# Copy to `.env` and edit. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# ── IMPORTANT: who actually reads this file ──────────────────────────────────────
#
#   docker compose   YES — Compose auto-loads a `.env` next to docker-compose.yml
#                          and substitutes ${VAR} in it.
#   python / make    NO  — the Python code reads the *process* environment only.
#                          Nothing calls load_dotenv(). Export the vars, or use
#                          `direnv`, or prefix the command.
#   vite / npm       NO  — Vite reads `web/.env`, not this one, and only honours
#                          names starting with VITE_. See the bottom section.
#
# The Python side deliberately does not auto-load a dotenv file. AUTOPSY_PROVIDER
# decides whether the pipeline spends money, and a file quietly flipping it to
# `live` because it happened to be on disk is the kind of surprise that shows up as
# a bill. Making it explicit costs one `export` and removes a whole class of
# accident.
#
# PowerShell:  $env:AUTOPSY_PROVIDER = "live"
# bash/zsh:    export AUTOPSY_PROVIDER=live
# one-shot:    AUTOPSY_PROVIDER=live make ablate


# ── Core ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Required to run anything from the repo root, because the packages are not
# installed into site-packages during development. `make` sets this for you.
PYTHONPATH=.

# offline | groq | openai | live
#
#   offline  A deterministic rule-based simulator. No network, no key, no cost.
#            The default, and what CI runs. Worth knowing: the simulator is bad at
#            hedging, so the silent-failure suite scores far worse offline (4 of 9 traps
#            handled) than on a real model (9 of 10). That is the simulator, not the
#            pipeline.
#   groq     Real open-weight models on Groq's free tier: `openai/gpt-oss-120b` to
#            generate, `llama-3.1-8b-instant` to rerank, `qwen/qwen3.6-27b` to judge.
#            Real LLM behaviour with no billing account. Groq serves no embeddings
#            endpoint at all, so the dense leg runs locally — see AUTOPSY_EMBEDDER.
#   openai   gpt-4o-mini everywhere. Costs money, roughly $0.0003 a question.
#   live     Anthropic + OpenAI. Costs money.
#
# Anything else is rejected at startup rather than silently falling back.
#
# ── The best free combination ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `provider` and `embedder` are independent axes, so you can have real embeddings
# without a key of any kind:
#
#   AUTOPSY_PROVIDER=offline
#   AUTOPSY_EMBEDDER=fastembed
#
# The simulator writes the answers while BGE-small does the embedding for real. The 3D
# embedding view then shows true geometry rather than a simulation, at zero cost. That
# pairing was broken until recently — `default_config()` took `embed_model` from the
# *provider* row, so overriding only the embedder handed fastembed the string
# "offline-concept" and it raised. Fixed, and pinned by tests/test_embedder_axis.py.
AUTOPSY_PROVIDER=offline


# ── Model credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# AUTOPSY_PROVIDER=groq. Free tier: https://console.groq.com/keys
#
#   generation  openai/gpt-oss-120b
#   rerank      llama-3.1-8b-instant
#   judge       qwen/qwen3.6-27b   <- a different family from the generator, on
#                                     purpose. Models favour their own family's
#                                     output, so a judge from the generator's family
#                                     inflates every number it produces.
#
# MEASURED free-tier limits, from the response headers on 2026-08-02:
#
#   x-ratelimit-limit-tokens     8000     per MINUTE
#   x-ratelimit-limit-requests   1000     per day
#
# At ~2k tokens of retrieved context per call that is about four calls a minute. A full
# `ablate -n 220` sweep will not fit; use `--core -n 15`.
#
# There is ALSO a daily token cap, and Groq does not expose it in any header. When it is
# exhausted the per-minute counters above still read healthy, so the failure looks like a
# rate limit that never clears no matter how long you wait. `is_daily_limit()` checks the
# provider's own body text rather than the counters, for exactly this reason.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# AUTOPSY_PROVIDER=live only.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=


# ── Embeddings — chosen separately from the chat provider ────────────────────────
#
# concept | fastembed | openai
#
#   concept    The offline simulator's concept bags. Free, deterministic, not a real
#              embedding model.
#   fastembed  BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 via ONNX, locally. Real embeddings, no key, no
#              GPU, ~130MB on first use. The default under `groq`, because Groq has
#              no embeddings endpoint at all.
#   openai     text-embedding-3-small. Costs money.
#
# Left unset, this follows the provider's default.
# AUTOPSY_EMBEDDER=fastembed
# AUTOPSY_EMBED_MODEL=BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5


# ── Gate — derive these, do not inherit them ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# The gate reads a raw similarity score, and every embedding model puts that score on
# its own scale. Concept-coverage runs 0–1 with a true floor at 0; BGE-small scores
# *unrelated* English at ~0.55. A threshold carried across models either passes
# everything or refuses everything, and the trace reports `gate: passed` either way.
#
# `python -m autopsy.cli calibrate-gate` measures all three signals against the
# corpus and prints the winner. On this corpus with BGE-small it found dense_top1 and
# fused_top1 both *overlap* (negative separation) while lexical_top1 separates
# cleanly — the opposite of the usual recommendation.
#
# AUTOPSY_GATE_READS=lexical_top1
# AUTOPSY_GATE_THRESHOLD=1.738


# ── Vector store ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# local | qdrant
#
# `local` is numpy in-process — no daemon, instant, and what the offline reports were
# produced with. `qdrant` is a real Qdrant collection.
AUTOPSY_VECTOR_BACKEND=local

# Qdrant has two shapes, and which one you get depends on which of these is set.
#
#   QDRANT_URL   a Qdrant server. Concurrent access, needs Docker or a hosted instance.
#   QDRANT_PATH  embedded on-disk collection via qdrant-client's local mode. No daemon,
#                no Docker. Same client API and the same in-query payload filters, but
#                it is the Python implementation rather than the Rust server, and it
#                takes an EXCLUSIVE FILE LOCK — one process at a time. With the API
#                server running, CLI commands will fail on that lock; either stop the
#                server or prefix the command with AUTOPSY_VECTOR_BACKEND=local.
#
# URL wins if both are set. Neither set, and `qdrant` defaults to embedded under
# corpus/index/qdrant.
#
# Both are commented out on purpose. QDRANT_URL used to ship uncommented here, which meant
# copying this file to `.env` and switching the backend to `qdrant` pointed the client at a
# server on localhost:6333 that does not exist — and because URL beats PATH, it silently
# skipped the embedded mode that needs no daemon. Leave them unset unless you are actually
# running a Qdrant server.
# QDRANT_URL=http://localhost:6333
# QDRANT_PATH=./corpus/index/qdrant


# ── API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Comma-separated. Explicit origins rather than `*`, so a wildcard cannot survive
# into a deployment by inertia.
AUTOPSY_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173


# ── Provenance ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Overrides the `code` field stamped into every trace's `versions` block. Leave unset
# outside CI: the code falls back to the git SHA, then to a hash of the Python
# sources. The counterfactual engine refuses to diff traces whose `versions` differ,
# so pinning this by hand disables a real safety check.
# AUTOPSY_CODE_VERSION=


# ── Frontend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These belong in `web/.env`, NOT here — Vite only reads its own root, and only
# exposes names prefixed with VITE_. Repeated here so the full set is in one place.
#
#   VITE_DEMO_ONLY=1              Static keyless build: replay pre-recorded traces
#                                 from web/src/demo/traces instead of calling the API.
#                                 docker-compose sets this as a build arg.
#   VITE_API_BASE=/api            Overrides the HTTP base. Default proxies to :8000.
#   VITE_WS_BASE=/stream          Overrides the websocket path.
